From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 13:31:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01144/11171] [conductor] In-process docs for GAP-5
 CROSS-EXAMPLE-CONSISTENCY SELECTOR upgrade (build against the logged GAP-5
 demo-underdetermination gap per the Missing-Verifier Gap Logging mandate):
 exp4001 logged GAP-5 (multiple demo-consistent programs disagree on the test
 = the verifier cannot select among them). Build a STRONGER discriminator than
 plain output-agreement: among induced demo-perfect programs, score each by
 (a) cross-DEMONSTRATION consistency (does it reproduce held-out demo pairs,
 leave-one-demo-out) and (b) SIBLING-INPUT agreement (do the candidate
 programs agree on perturbed/sibling inputs). Measure whether this lifts
 precision and/or coverage over plain final-grid output-agreement on the SAME
 ARC-2 chain-feasible pool (reuse the cached induced programs; NO new codex
 calls if the saved programs suffice). The cleanest off-the-shelf design
 (arXiv:2604.02434 cross-example consistency filtering). A new
 registry-eligible discriminator that closes a logged gap is direct progress
 on Carnot's core.

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
